Flutter apps, three features that would be suitable responsibilities for a junior Flutter developer during their first three months are:

1. Login/Registration Screens

A junior developer could build or maintain:

Login screen
Registration screen
Form validation
Password fields
Error messages
Connecting the screen to a login API
2. List and Detail Screens

A junior developer could work on:

Displaying a list of items using Flutter widgets
Fetching data from an API
Creating cards/list items
Opening a detail page when an item is selected
Handling loading and empty states
3. Profile Editing

A junior developer could implement:

User profile screen
Edit profile form
Updating name, email, or other information
Form validation
Sending updated information to the backend API
Testing the feature and fixing UI bugs
Conclusion

These tasks are suitable for a junior Flutter developer because they provide practical experience with Flutter UI, Dart, API integration, form handling, navigation, testing, and debugging without requiring them to design the entire application architecture themselves.
